WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
Have you ever wondered what the world's longest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.280
ongoing war is? I have been fascinated&nbsp;
with this border for a very long time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.840
and a few months ago I went to just go see&nbsp;
what it looked like and I found something kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:17.100
of insane. So one of the major ways that North&nbsp;
and South Korea fight each other today is with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:24.180
speakers. There is an ongoing battle between&nbsp;
North and South Korea on who can blast the loudest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:30.420
propaganda or music at each other. South Koreans&nbsp;
will blast like K-Pop and all sorts of things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.160
Sometimes they'll just like make fun of North&nbsp;
Koreans on a hot day for not having, like, movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.060
theaters they can go into with air conditioning.&nbsp;
North Korea, on the other hand, will just blast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:44.880
like communist propaganda like these operas from&nbsp;
the Soviet times. And they will get so loud to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.620
the point where it will become like damaging, like&nbsp;
will break glass. So they've actually had to like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.460
like come to some agreement to come to the&nbsp;
table and be like, no more speaker wars.

